    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0394" n="306" xml:id="pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/419: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-08T17:00:00-04:00">June 8, 1933—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. You are instructed to proceed with negotiations for the revision of the
                    commercial treaty with Cuba in connection with the Administration’s policy of
                    obtaining reciprocal trade agreements with other countries. The treaty will be
                    submitted to the Senate at the next session of Congress. Public announcement
                    that these instructions have been sent you will be made by the Department
                    probably tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
